==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Michelangelo Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Quizmaster Cat''' when obtained from the [[NEO Darkness Heaven]] (cannot drop in the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Bronze Cat is a decent support unit against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]] in the early-game, when you lack alternatives. She can be very useful against tough Metal enemies like [[Metal Cyclone]] or [[Sir Metal Seal]], and has the health to tank one or two hits from tougher Metal enemies. Overall, however, [[Clockwork Cat (Rare Cat)|Clockwork Cat]] and [[Drumcorps Cat (Rare Cat)|Drumcorps Cat]] are still more reliable. Aside from reliability, knockbacks are a double-edged sword against Metal enemies. On the one hand, the ability to keep them from advancing is generally nice, especially due to the lack of Metal backliners. However, there are some situations where doing so is disadvantageous, such as knocking a potential target out of [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]]'s range while she goes through her long attack animation, or knocking a more threatening enemy behind more annoying peons such as [[Metal Doge]]. As [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] already tend to rely on heavy luck, Bronze Cat may end up being counterproductive instead.

Bronze Cat's [[Cat Combo]]s can see some usage in Metal stages, where [[Eye of the Storm (Combo)|Eye of the Storm]] and [[Art History (Combo)|Art History]] can raise the effective HP of [[Rope Jump Cat (Rare Cat)|Noodle Cats]] and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] respectively. Otherwise Art History finds usage in helping many great tanks/meatshields like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]] and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]].

==='''True Form'''===
Quizmaster Cat gains 30 more range, more attack power, and an extra 10% chance to knockback Metal enemies but has a significantly slower attack rate. The range buff can be helpful in some certain cases, like now being able to outrange [[Super Metal Hippoe]], but the attack buff can be ignored as this unit is not meant for general use, and the attack rate penalty outweighs the marginally higher activation chance, greatly reducing its consistency.

